text:
The plate holds scrambled eggs with a small herb leaf. The plate is about 25 cm wide, and the egg pile covers roughly 8 by 14 cm. At a thickness of about 2–3 cm, that comes to about 120–150 g of eggs.

Scrambled eggs cooked with some fat run about 150–170 kcal per 100 g. At 130 g, that gives roughly 205 kcal.

